{
 "BINDING": {
  "BOARD_SCHEMA_FINDING": {
   "disposition": "derivation disclosed per board via TEAMS_DERIVED_FROM_GAME_KEY rather than performed silently. Carrying away/home as MLB fields is the real fix and is NOT applied here \u2014 the board is frozen under R3.",
   "how_it_surfaced": "the first pass refused all 15 MLB rows with MISSING_IDENTITY_FIELD while all 4 WNBA rows bound cleanly. The asymmetry is the board schema, not the relay.",
   "severity": "BOUNDED. An archive row brings its own away/home, so TEAMS_REVERSED can still fire there. The narrow exposure is that a game key BUILT backwards at freeze time would have nothing on the board to contradict it \u2014 the same shape as the LAD@DET starter reversal: one source, nothing to disagree with it.",
   "what": "the MLB board stores away and home ONLY inside the composite game key (\"mlb:CIN@CHC\"). The WNBA board stores them as explicit fields. Two of the six binding-contract fields are therefore not independently held on an MLB board."
  },
  "CORRECTION": {
   "effect_on_the_grades": "NONE of the recomputed metrics change. They were always computed by joining the frozen board to the relayed finals on the game key, which is the identity match. What changes is the WARRANT published beside them: from 'bound, gradable' to 'identity-matched, date unestablished, descriptive only'.",
   "how_it_was_found": "an adversarial audit of this repo's retrieval surface, not by re-reading the output. The record and the card both looked correct.",
   "what_is_true_instead": "IDENTITY matches for every game: each relayed score attaches to a canonical id that is on the board with the same matchup. That is a real and useful claim. It is strictly weaker than binding: it does not establish that the score is that game's score, and it establishes nothing about the date.",
   "what_was_published": "the 2026-08-28 full card and the first version of this record published RESULT_BINDING_PASS = 15/15 (mlb) and 4/4 (wnba), DATE_COHERENCE_PASS identical, and gradable = true for both cohorts.",
   "why_that_was_wrong": "this module stamped result_date from its own SLATE_DATE constant. That is the missing field being MANUFACTURED so the row would bind \u2014 the same evasion selftest B1 exists to refuse, performed one level up where B1 could not see it. The counter compared a constant against the board's own date and was structurally incapable of failing. Had the wrong night's finals been relayed \u2014 the exact 2026-08-27 P0 \u2014 it would still have read 15/15."
  },
  "VERDICT": "NOT BOUND \u2014 and it never was. See CORRECTION below.",
